OL,3,GNEWSACourt of Appeal hearing residents'
OL,4,Aparade challenge
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe decision to allow a controversial
OL,7,FOrange Order parade down a
OL,8,Fpredominantly nationalist road is being
OL,9,Fchallenged at Belfast's Court of Appeal
OL,10,Fthis morning
OL,12,FThere have been eight days of deadlock
OL,13,Fover the parade down Portadown's
OL,14,FGarvaghy Road since it was decided it
OL,15,Fcould proceed, a decision that reopened
OL,16,Fwhat was once Northern Ireland's most
OL,17,Fbitter parading disputes
OL,19,FResidents and protesters have
OL,20,Fperiodically blocked the road and
OL,21,Fmaintained a presence there for more
OL,22,Fthan a week
OL,23,APub: 05-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/3
OL,24,ANext PageB NI NewsC Reg TVF On This Day
FL,412,410,260,120,0,100
PN,41102
SC,0002
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F411A1791194152
OL,1,W5j 5Q7k jjs%wsj  w{j#57i
OL,2,W//%*// //%Q%* ** %-,*,$%** %-& (,,,,,,,
OL,3,GNEWSACourt of Appeal hearing residents'
OL,4,Aparade challenge
OL,5,
OL,6,FMeanwhile Orangemen have repeatedly
OL,7,Fattempted to complete the march but
OL,8,Fbeen have been turned back by police
OL,9,Fdue to it being unsafe to proceed
OL,11,FResidents are taking the case to the
OL,12,FCourt of Appeal, arguing the Parades
OL,13,FCommission - the organisation that
OL,14,Fapproved the march - did not give an
OL,15,Faccurate representation of the Police
OL,16,FService of Northern Ireland's (PSNI's)
OL,17,Fevidence
OL,23,APub: 05-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG2/3
OL,24,ANext PageB NI NewsC Reg TVF On This Day
FL,412,410,260,120,0,100
PN,41103
SC,0003
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F411A1791194152
OL,1,W5j 5Q7k jjs%wsj  w{j#57i
OL,2,W//%*// //%Q%* ** %-,*,$%** %-& (,,,,,,,
OL,3,GNEWSACourt of Appeal hearing residents'
OL,4,Aparade challenge
OL,5,
OL,6,FIn the mid-to-late 1990s, the dispute
OL,7,Fabout the Orange Order parade from
OL,8,FDrumcree Church down the Garvaghy Road
OL,9,Fcreated yearly stand-offs, accompanied
OL,10,Fwith riots, roadblock and killings -
OL,11,Fread more about the history of the
OL,12,Fdispute
OL,14,FWith hundreds of people on the street,
OL,15,Fand rival groups not far apart, there's
OL,16,Fhuge relief nobody has yet been hurt
OL,17,Fbut the challenge is in making sure it
OL,18,Fstays that way, writes BBC News NI
OL,19,Fcommunities correspondent Mark Simpson
OL,23,APub: 05-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG3/3
OL,24,ANext PageB NI NewsC Reg TVF On This Day
